<title>USA: FCOJ futures close firmer but still within range.</title>
<headline>FCOJ futures close firmer but still within range.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>NYCE frozen concentrated orange juice futures closed higher for the second straight session, buoyed by local and speculative buying, traders said.</p>
<p>The buying broke through stops around 114.00 cents a lb and carried the market to its highs.</p>
<p>November settled up 2.85 at 114.80, having ranged from 114.90 to 111.95. Resistance was seen between 115.00 and 116.00. The back months finished 1.60 to 1.00 higher.</p>
<p>Volume was estimated at 1,000 lots.</p>
<p>--Suzanne Rostler, New York Commodities 212-859-1646</p>
